==About==
The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series. '''PUBG''' was announced as part of the line-up on February 26, 2024. <ref name="EWC PUBG">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESWCgg/status/1762070002134294543|title=Korea, where we droppin’?|date=2024-02-26|author='''Esports World Cup'''|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>
:''See [https://liquipedia.net/esports/Esports_World_Cup/2024 here] to read about the Esports World Cup 2024, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

===Format===
* '''Group Stage:''' ''August 21th - 23rd'' <ref name="EWC PUBG announced">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/ESWCgg/status/1795756977378759037|title=It’s time to share more about @PUBGEsports at the #EsportsWorldCup tournament!|date=2024-05-29|author='''Esports World Cup'''|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>
** 18 matches across 3 groups (each team plays 12 matches)
*** {{bgcolortext|up|''Top 16 teams}} advance to the Grand Finals''
*** {{bgcolortext|down|''Bottom 8 teams}} will be eliminated''

* '''Grand Finals:''' ''August 24th - 25th'' 
** 12 matches 
*** Grand Finals will now be played in the standard SUPER format instead of Match Point <ref name="EWC MP">{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/1821562082795393497|title=We have an update regarding the format for #EsportsWorldCup PUBG: BATTLEGROUNDS.|date=2024-08-08|author='''Esports World Cup'''|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref>

