The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series. 

On October 8th, 2025, '''PUBG: Battlegrounds''' was announced to continue being part of the game titles' line-up for the third iteration of the '''EWC'''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.instagram.com/p/DPjXCYrgsQL/ |title=We’re coming back in 2026 with a squad of the most prestigious esports titles 🏆 |date=2025-10-08 |publisher='''Esports World Cup'''}}</ref> It was originally planned to be hosted in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, but was moved to Paris, France on May 20.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/2057121960623006162|title=Esports World Cup 2026 is coming to Paris|author=Esports World Cup|author-link=Esports World Cup|date=2026-05-20}}</ref>

==About==

===Format===
* '''Group Stage:''''' July 21st - 23rd, 2026
** Prior to the Group Stage, 24 teams will be divided into THREE groups: Group A, Group B & Group C
** Each group plays against other groups in round robin system ('''''AvsB, AvsC & BvsC''''')
** 6 matches per Group match-up ('''''In total, each team played 12 matches equally''''')
** Teams' placements are based on all 18 matches
*** {{Bgcolortext|up|'''''Top 16 teams'''''}} advances to '''Finals'''
*** {{Bgcolortext|down|'''''Bottom 8 teams'''''}} are eliminated
* '''Grand Finals:''''' July 24th - 26th, 2026
** 16 teams.
** Maximum of 18 matches (6 each day).
*** '''Smash Rule''' is applied on Day 3 of Finals Stage.
**** {{Jib_mid_season_start|title=''For more detailed information on the format, '''click here'''.''}}

{{box|start}}
* Teams would play using regular tournament rules on the first two days
* '''Match Point''' will be determined after the end of Day 2
** The Match Point for this stage is '''Total Points of 1st place after Day 2 + 10 Points'''.
* Upon entering Day 3, the tournament will be playing under '''Smash Rule'''
* Once a team reaches the Match Point threshold, that team will become '''"Match Point Eligible"''' for the subsequent matches.
* The '''first team''' to secure a {{WWCD}}&nbsp;{{Abbr/WWCD}} after they are '''"Match Point Eligible"''' will automatically be crowned the Winner/Champion of the stage.
* Maximum number of matches to be played is '''{{{maxmatch|18}}} matches'''; thus if none of the '''"Match Point Eligible"''' teams were able to claim a {{WWCD}}&nbsp;{{Abbr/WWCD}}, then the team with the most points will emerge as the Winner/Champion.
**'''''Therefore, the lowest possible number of games to be played is 14 (reaching Match Point in Game 13 and win the following game).
{{box|end}}
{{TextDropdown|end}}

{{Jib_mid_season_end}}

